## Notes

Fill the `{{…}}` placeholders during `/bootstrap`. Keep this REQ short — it is a compass,
not a specification.

The acceptance criterion deliberately checks **initialization**, not function: on day one
there is no behaviour to assert, and the north star only ever claimed the project exists
and is coherent. `/bootstrap` closes by running `steward checkpoint`, so the engine — not a
skill — verifies this and lands REQ-001 as `done`. Everything the project actually *does*
is the subject of REQ-002 onward.

Do not widen this criterion to the full test suite. The engine's capture check re-runs
every named acceptance test from a bare extract of the committed tree — no virtualenv,
nothing installed — so a whole-suite criterion here passes in the working tree and then
fails the gate for reasons that have nothing to do with the north star. The project's real
build and test commands belong in `.devsteward/config.yaml`, where the develop gate runs
them as `verify.full_suite` for every REQ.
